DIZZYING SPEEDRUN — INTENTIONAL KINETICS CUT

Duration: 25s
Aspect: 16:9 cinematic
FPS: 48
Style: Hyper-kinetic sci-fi war montage
Genre: Industrial warfare / vertical ocean megastructure chaos

HARD TIMING LAW

✅ ALL SCENES < 2.0s
✅ NO SCENE > 1.8s
✅ MOST SCENES 0.5–1.4s

Cuts are fast because threats force them, not arbitrarily.

RULE ZERO 

❌ NO STATIC
❌ NO HOLDS
❌ NO ESTABLISHING SHOTS
❌ NO COMPLETE ACTIONS

The video starts mid-maneuver.
The viewer is already late.
Cuts interrupt understanding — but always after a cause.

CORE IDEA (LOCKED)

There is no plan.
There is no strategy.
Only reaction.
Thinking is slower than dying.

CAMERA LAW — INTENTIONAL PANIC

FPV / cockpit-adjacent POV only
Constant forward velocity
Camera motion is ALWAYS motivated by one of the following (MANDATORY):
Incoming threat
Structural constraint
Shockwave displacement
Collision avoidance
Sudden vector loss

❌ No decorative shake
❌ No random whip-pans

Movement Rules
Whip-pans occur only when tracking or evading a threat
Rolls occur only to clear obstacles or survive blast pressure
Yaw and pitch respond to geometry, not emotion
Micro-jitter = engine vibration + airflow stress (subtle, continuous)
Brief micro-stability (0.2–0.4s) allowed only while lining up escape vectors
The camera never “dances.”
It executes survival corrections.

LENS & FRAMING (CONTROLLED AGGRESSION)
24mm wide → corridor runs, water skims, structural threading
35mm → pursuit chaos, missile evasion
50mm → compression during dives or near-collisions
Foreground occlusion is intentional:
Pipes, cables, antennae, wreckage cross frame to prove proximity
Never more than one dominant occluder per shot
Lens breathing occurs only under acceleration or G-force spikes.

PHYSICS RULES (UNCHANGED, STRICT)
Everything has mass, speed, inertia
Explosions displace air, water, debris, and camera
Shockwaves buffet the POV violently
Wreckage persists and becomes obstacles
Missiles curve late and aggressively

❌ No float
❌ No slow motion
❌ No cosmetic explosions

Momentum always wins.

AUDIO — VIOLENCE WITH STRUCTURE
BGM
Hybrid PHONK × Mad-Max war score
132–142 BPM
Distorted 808s, metallic percussion, industrial war drums
Mix Discipline
Bass hits align with physical impacts
Engines surge during acceleration, drop during evasive rolls
Silence fragments (0.1–0.2s) allowed only after shockwaves

Radio
Single-word bursts only:
“LEFT!”
“NOW!”
“CLEAR—” (cut)

WORLD LOGIC (UNCHANGED)

This is not a battlefield.
This is infrastructure under stress.

The city is a vertical logistics artery.
Airspace is narrow and hostile by design.
Threats emerge from architecture, not villains.
Destruction is operational, not emotional.

SCENE FLOW — CAUSE → CAMERA → CUT
SCENE 1 — 0.0–1.2s

Mid-dive FPV.
Camera stable for 0.3s → incoming fire forces pitch drop.

SCENE 2 — 1.2–2.1s (0.9s)

Missile enters peripheral vision → hard yaw to evade.

SCENE 3 — 2.1–3.4s (1.3s)

